<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anseung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 670–683</span> · Also known as Ansung</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anseung was a member of the Goguryeo royal family whom Silla recognised as king of Goguryeo in 670, after the fall of Goguryeo to Silla and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. Silla settled him and his followers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iksan">Geummajeo</a>, modern Iksan, where his state was later called Bodeok. He married a Silla noblewoman and in 683 was moved to the Silla capital, after which his kingdom was abolished.</p></div>
